note "stagger: a stagger numbers only children with an enter (owner, decisions.md stagger): the subject, with none, is at rest and takes no turn, so tag1 and tag2 each start one turn earlier (60 Hz: tag1 k2->k1, tag2 k4->k2; 144 Hz: k5->k1, k9->k5), with the same opacity and offset trajectories. Read again (stagger review): keyframes keeps playing, so unlike the other stagger cells this run has its reference's tick count (57 at 60 Hz, 128 at 144 Hz) and is not shifted; diffed block to block, only the rows of tag1 and tag2 differ, every other node and surface is the same tick for tick"
